{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1528403-quintessence-spending-spells","id":1528403,"title":"Quintessence spending spells","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-11T17:05:49-08:00","id":1528403,"title":"Quintessence spending spells","content":"We know a mage can spend 1 quintessence to create something from scratch, heal aggravated by 1 level per point, inflict and resist aggr, reduce arete difficulty and so on... But it's unclear how much is needed for each spells.<br /> <br /> Let's take them with few exemples:<br /> -You give quintessence to you friends so he can soak and inflict aggr damage, does it work like quintessence weapon? One attack/soak per point given, or does the number of point define the duration?<br /> <br /> -You summon a living being, knowing that human sized posess 10points of quintessence do you need to invest 10 point to build one from scratch?<br /> <br /> -According to the book &quot;How do you do that?&quot; some effect need quintessence to continue to work, like pure energy shield, flame whip... What other kind of spells need that energy? A delfective effect using force that increase difficulty to be hit for exemple? Do you have exemple of spells you would ask for quintessence to be maintained?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T19:47:01-08:00","id":1528406,"title":"","content":"Most spells have an up-front cost. It's not really clear if defensive spells require per use like offensive ones do, but considering healing/damage works that way, I would argue it does.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, the easiest way to deal with ongoing spells are the Pattern Bleed rules, since the way to keep from taking damage from Pattern Bleed is to spend quintessence instead. Pattern Bleed is also something with more guidance of when it applies, so you don't have to wing it nearly as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T22:51:51-08:00","id":1528408,"title":"","content":"If what I've read in a few forum conversations recently is correct (trying to get a handle on some of this stuff myself), you don't always need to spend a <u>Point</u> of Quintessence to make something from nothing. A lot of the time you are using &quot;free&quot; Quintessence that is just floating around. I think the rule is you need to spend a Point of Quintessence for something that will be consuming/outputting energy of some kind without any other fuel source, or if you're making something especially large/powerful.<br /> <br /> A few examples:<br /> <br /> 1) If you used Matter to make a piece of wood, you would not need to spend a Point of Quintessence, you just need Prime 2 to gather up and use the &quot;free&quot; Quintessence floating around.<br /> <br /> 2) If you used Forces to light the piece of wood you just made on fire, you would not need to spend a Point of Quintessence; you could light the fire with &quot;free&quot; Quintessence by adding Prime 2, and if will be burning the wood for fuel after the initial moment of combustion.<br /> <br /> 3) If you wanted to use Forces to make a ball of fire that would just hover in the air, and continue burning with no fuel, <u>then</u> you would need to spend a Point of Quintessence to &quot;fuel&quot; it.<br /> <br /> Making an entire person would probably require multiple Points of Quintessence, but that's not something I've looked at very much so I can't say for sure. I'd bet you could find the rules either in the Core or HDYDT if someone on here doesn't get you a response quick.<br /> <br /> A lot of the spells you see in HDYDT that require expending a Point of Quintessence for things like Energy Shields are in the specific case of Prime Effects, from what I recall. A Mage that is manipulating Matter or Forces generally has the &quot;stuff&quot; that they want to manipulate out in front of them. But for a Prime Mage who doesn't have those Spheres, making a shield or weapon out of pure Primal energy may be the best option available. But they need &quot;stuff&quot; to work with, and that's why they spend the Point of Quintessence, to have &quot;stuff&quot; to turn into a shield, weapon, etc.<br /> <br /> If you aren't being instructed to spend a Point of Quintessence by the rulebooks themselves, then ultimately the question of when it's necessary will probably be up to your Storyteller. It may be better to ask them to get an idea of what to expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T08:05:33-08:00","id":1528414,"title":"","content":"HDYDT makes a lot of arbitrary and often nonsensical calls, though, so you have to take a lot of care in how you use it. For instance on pg 38 it suggests powering a fire, lightning bolt, or force field might require 1-5 quintessence per turn and requires Prime 3 for the channeling and there is no mention at all of Prime 2 or using 'free' quintessence.<br /> <br /> Considering that one of the abilities of Prime 2 is Fuel Pattern, it should be reasonable (if vulgar) to make an eternal flame using just Forces 3/Prime 2 and no quintessence surcharge. Perhaps there's a section somewhere I've forgotten about that explicitly limits Prime 2. Let me know if you find one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T10:17:51-08:00","id":1528417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1528403-quintessence-spending-spells?p=1528414#post1528414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HDYDT makes a lot of arbitrary and often nonsensical calls, though, so you have to take a lot of care in how you use it. For instance on pg 38 it suggests powering a fire, lightning bolt, or force field might require 1-5 quintessence per turn and requires Prime 3 for the channeling and there is no mention at all of Prime 2 or using 'free' quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok so most of the indications of HDYDT are just put there without basic rule to tell how it's possible..... so you would stick to the basic lines of M20 about quintessence use in that case (and really this would be better, hdydt has made a mess in my head, trying to understand when something work and when it's not). Can't recall the section about prime 2 limits, it was in M20 or HDYDT?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T11:09:33-08:00","id":1528425,"title":"","content":"HDYDT and M20 seem to have drastically higher Quint costs than revised. Seems a bit no sensible really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T07:07:48-08:00","id":1528647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1528403-quintessence-spending-spells?p=1528417#post1528417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok so most of the indications of HDYDT are just put there without basic rule to tell how it's possible..... so you would stick to the basic lines of M20 about quintessence use in that case (and really this would be better, hdydt has made a mess in my head, trying to understand when something work and when it's not). Can't recall the section about prime 2 limits, it was in M20 or HDYDT?</div> </div> </div> </div>The majority of the time I use HDYDT as an indication of what <i>not</i> do do. That's not even a joke at this point. If I find myself in agreement with HDYDT I double check my thinking. A while ago in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511445-sphere-oddities-in-m20\">Sphere Oddities in M20</a> I went through all the inconsistencies, bad examples, and bad explanations of spell requirements I found in the M20 core. I intended to continue on to give the same treatment to HDYDT but the problems were coming in so fast I gave up.<br /> <br /> In places where M20 has nothing about a particular subject it is sometimes useful to see some considerations that might need addressing. Even there, though, I'd go back to M20 and work out how to address those issues myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T08:27:59-08:00","id":1528652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1528403-quintessence-spending-spells?p=1528647#post1528647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In places where M20 has nothing about a particular subject it is sometimes useful to see some considerations that might need addressing. Even there, though, I'd go back to M20 and work out how to address those issues myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, hdydt only worth for those rules that were put of M20, for example, how mich weight you can lift with forces. It has some good rules for combat too (not the chi shit!!!)<br /> I dismiss anything that goes agaimst M20 or how Mage used to work since ever.<br /> <br /> To answer OP no you don't need to spend quint to create from scratch. The mage uses &quot;free&quot; quint from the environment. A case could be made if you plan to use MUCH more energy than there could be as free quint, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T15:30:52-08:00","id":1528685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1528403-quintessence-spending-spells?p=1528652#post1528652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To answer OP no you don't need to spend quint to create from scratch. The mage uses &quot;free&quot; quint from the environment. A case could be made if you plan to use MUCH more energy than there could be as free quint, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? You don't need quint? In M20 p.538, however, it is said you must spend quint to create effect of life, matter and force from nothing <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T19:38:35-08:00","id":1528699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1528403-quintessence-spending-spells?p=1528685#post1528685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? You don't need quint? In M20 p.538, however, it is said you must spend quint to create effect of life, matter and force from nothing</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a bit of a change from Mage Revised. For revised, if you are creating a fireball, etc, you don't need Quint for it because you are drawing Quint from the Tapestry itself to fuel it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T21:45:47-08:00","id":1528702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furoan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1528403-quintessence-spending-spells?p=1528699#post1528699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is actually a bit of a change from Mage Revised. For revised, if you are creating a fireball, etc, you don't need Quint for it because you are drawing Quint from the Tapestry itself to fuel it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm pretty sure that it was clarified that the Revised version also applies to M20, in a Q&amp;A with Phil Brucato IIRC? It's a problem around the word 'Quintessence' being used in too many different fashions in M20 without clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T07:20:29-08:00","id":1528711,"title":"","content":"The wording on page 537 is unfortunate as it seems to refer to both the spending of personal points of quintessence and the use of the substance of quintessence with no clear indication of when it is using one or the other. Based on the wording the chart is listing things that involve the substance of quintessence, which is why the paragraph immediately after the chart specifies one entry as also requiring <i>points</i> of quintessence. <br /> <br /> Special shoutout to the last entry on the chart: [b]Facilitating the many uses of the Prime Sphere[b] which is so general as to be pointless, is only there for padding, and only even fits because an odd wording that reverses the definition of the sphere. It would be like opening a biology textbook and seeing the following qualities of plants:<ul><li>They produce food through photosynthesis</li> <li>They have cell nuclei.</li> <li>They are studied by botanists.</li> </ul>It's technically true, sure, but its only true because of the definition of botanists, not the definition of plants.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T08:26:17-08:00","id":1528799,"title":"","content":"Assuming the quintessence used comes from the environment, the only way a mage can interact with it is with Prime 5, or prime 4 to use it from an object if my reading is correct, otherwise you would need to drain it from a clear source like nodes, tass and other with prime 3.<br /> <br /> Considering this it is unlikly the raw would let you cast something without your own quintessence being involved, or i miss an important point in M20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T09:14:10-08:00","id":1528804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1528403-quintessence-spending-spells?p=1528799#post1528799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming the quintessence used comes from the environment, the only way a mage can interact with it is with Prime 5, or prime 4 to use it from an object if my reading is correct, otherwise you would need to drain it from a clear source like nodes, tass and other with prime 3.<br /> <br /> Considering this it is unlikly the raw would let you cast something without your own quintessence being involved, or i miss an important point in M20</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the post that was my best source on this. I can't access the FB page, but it includes the relevant information:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/756758-how-do-you-do-that-hdydt-fan-edition?p=758643#post758643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in this Facebook Post in the M20 Kickstarter Alumni Group:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/305772249570487/permalink/571348219679554/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/3057...1348219679554/</a><br /> <br /> Not sure if everyone will be able to access that since it is a closed group but here's what was said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Me: I have a question that I hope Phil Brucato might be able to answer. Do you need to spend a point of Quintessence every time you conjure something from nothing? Or do you draw ambient Quintessence from the environment to do this? I've received contradictory answers about this on forums. Thought I'd try to go right to the horse's mouth. Thanks in advance!<br /> <br /> Phil Brucato: No, you don't need to spend a point of Quintessence. </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Link to the thread in question: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/756758-how-do-you-do-that-hdydt-fan-edition/page2\">How Do **YOU** Do That? (HDYDT Fan Edition)</a><br /> \u200b<br /> There was another thread I found that went a lot more into the different ways that the word &quot;Quintessence&quot; has been used throughout various editions, and how it might apply in cases where M20 was ambiguous. I'll provide a link to that as well if I can track it down. But Word Of God is that you can conjure stuff out of thin air with Prime 2 <b>without</b> spending a Point of Quintessence, at least much of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T09:28:12-08:00","id":1528806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1528403-quintessence-spending-spells?p=1528799#post1528799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming the quintessence used comes from the environment, the only way a mage can interact with it is with Prime 5, or prime 4 to use it from an object if my reading is correct, otherwise you would need to drain it from a clear source like nodes, tass and other with prime 3.<br /> <br /> Considering this it is unlikly the raw would let you cast something without your own quintessence being involved, or i miss an important point in M20</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime 2 is the rank to divert quintessence into new forms. The mage can pull flows of quintessence from wherever it is quintessence flows from and use that to weave new patterns. This is why all 'creation from nothing' spells involve Prime 2. Note that this quintessence is not usable in other ways yet. Until higher ranks it cannot be converted into points of quintessence, nor can points of be converted into free flowing quintessence. Thus, not only does this not cost points of quintessence, it <i>can't</i> cost quintessence. A mage with only Prime 2 can't spend quintessence this way even if he wants to.<br /> <br /> Prime 3 is the rank at which mages are able to manipulate points of quintessence, but not alter it. Usually this means they can only access quintessence that is in the right form, like that in nodes and tass. This is also the level where they can move those points into other patterns to enhance them, Since they can't change the quintessence at this point this is not altering a pattern so much as charging it or perfecting it. <br /> <br /> Prime 4 is when mages can convert the quintessence bound in patterns into usable points of quintessence, and vice versa. This is the level where a mage could start using personal quintessence for 'creation from nothing' though I really don't know why he would want to.<br /> <br /> Prime 5 is when mages can pull quintessence out of anything, including ambient flows of quintessence they used in Prime 2. Only now can they","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T09:30:16-08:00","id":1528808,"title":"","content":"That was supposed to be: &quot;Only now can they use that ambient quintessence for anything other than powering new patterns.&quot; I can't edit it or it will get hidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T16:43:23-08:00","id":1528956,"title":"","content":"So the only case you spend quint is when you want to reduce arete difficulty, create wonders, reinforce paterns (can't find how long it last, 1 round per point maybe?), powering energy weapons...<br /> Anything else the book may have misspelled about quint cost and expenditure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T14:51:13-08:00","id":1529175,"title":"","content":"Healing aggravated damage, dealing aggravated damage, imbuing patterns with the ability to deal or resist aggravated damage, reduce magical difficulty, create wonders, create weapons or attacks from pure quintessence, resist void adaptation, fuel advanced countermagic and antimagic. <br /> <br /> The rules about using prime to create weapons and add aggravated damage to attacks are quite inconsistent. Sometimes it is one point per attack, sometimes it is one point per turn, and sometimes it is one point per damage. It sounds like an editing problem. I suspect that there were thoughts on adding aggravated damage to spells, thoughts on adding them to spells, thoughts on adding them to weapons, and thoughts on summoning magic weapons, but there was no real attempt to make them consistent with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T02:44:44-08:00","id":1529808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1528403-quintessence-spending-spells?p=1529175#post1529175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The rules about using prime to create weapons and add aggravated damage to attacks are quite inconsistent. Sometimes it is one point per attack, sometimes it is one point per turn, and sometimes it is one point per damage. It sounds like an editing problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would you chose? I was going for turn base duration for weapons reinforcement (to soak or deall aggr) and per attack for energy weapons, for living being maybe 1 scene duration for each point since quint will mix with vital energy of the being","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}